> Dlvl:27 $:0  HP:197(197) Pw:218(218) AC:-11 Xp:22/20053979 T:42061

You want that AC below -20 before going through Gehennom, goal is -30
or so before the ascension run.  Polypiling scrolls or writing them w/
magic markers is possible.

> a blessed amulet of life saving (being worn)

I prefer ESP but if it's your first time this deep life saving is a
better choice.

> the blessed Eye of the Aethiopica
> the rustproof +0 Fire Brand
> the rustproof +0 Magicbane (weapon in hand)

You want to enchant Magicbane up to +7 (you'll kill things a lot faster
that way than leaving it at lower enchantment for the weird effects).

But mainly you're using it for automatic 1-turn Elbereth and curse
resistance.

> a blessed fireproof +2 pair of speed boots (being worn)

If you have haste self, you should go w/ jumping boots.  haste self
will stack up more and more turns the more you cast it, so you can
easily stay very fast that way.  And jumping boots can get you going
2-3 times as fast.

> a blessed greased rustproof +2 helm of brilliance (being worn)

Good target for enchant armor.

> a blessed rustproof +2 pair of gauntlets of power (being worn)

Ditch these, you want to have no spell failure.  Dexterity or leather
gloves are better.

> 6 cursed scrolls of teleportation

Keep your stash of stuff in Sokoban.  Use these scrolls to get up there
and the Eye to get back down to Vlad's tower once you find it.  Also
use these as emergency escape tools.

> a blessed scroll of charging

Charge the wand of wishing now.

> an uncursed ring of regeneration (on right hand)
> an uncursed ring of sustain ability (on left hand)

Ditch these.  You want free action, slow digestion, conflict, and
levitation.  Always wear the former, switch the latter based on need
(conflict is a major help).

> 7 blessed wax candles

Put these in the bag or in your stash so they don't get melted.

> I have a lot more food in the bag.  I have a stash of about 50,000zm on
> lvl18 (thanks to a little trip to the Ft).

There's a priest on the level below the Castle that you can give your
gold to if you make it across the level.

>  Lots more wands (espeically
> magic misslle, striking, and teleport).

Hoard those /teleport, and always keep at least 1 in main inventory.

> I do have a magic marker and a few blank scrolls.

I'd write blessed charging (if the marker hasn't been recharged) then
as many enchant armor as possible.

>  I lost most of my scrolls and potions in the BoH accident, I have
> a couple of ID scrolls, two holy waters, and an unholy
> water.

You'll find lots in Gehennom.  Be careful with them.  And you probably
want to explore Gehennom more thoroughly than most people would since
you're trying to replenish your supplies.

>  Also I have not been crowned inspite of a number of #offers

Good, you really don't want to be crowned.

> I've got a scroll of charging so I could recharge the wand and get some
> wishes.  If I do that what should i wish for?

Save the wishes for now.

I'd use up the marker on enchant armor, then head down to the Valley
and cautiously clear it out to get to the priest and buy protection.
It shouldn't be too hard at that point, and you can use Magicbane to
engrave E in one turn (do this liberally) and use cursed ?teleport or
the Eye to escape if it really gets hairy.

The priest'll get you another 5 AC minimum with your gold, maybe as
much as 8.

> Now the horrors of Gehennom.  First, am I ready?  From the spoilers
> I've read, I don't think so.  Hp and Pw seem awfully low.

More Pw would be nice.  The Hp are fine, I usually have about 250 when
I ascend.  More for a first ascension is a good idea, but just make
sure you amass some !Full Healing and

